data.answer_preview:
The race condition occurs because when the payment provider retries, the webhook processes the same seat-add event twice before the database update commits, causing duplicate charges. To fix this idempotently in PostgreSQL, use a unique constraint on the event ID and insert with "ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING". This way, if the event is already processed, the insert is ignored, preventing double charges. Example SQL: 

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX unique_event_id ON seat_add_events(event_id);

INSERT INTO seat_add_events(event_id, account_id, seats, processed_at) VALUES ($1, $2, $3, NOW()) ON CONFLICT (event_id) DO NOTHING;

This approach ensures the event is processed only once despite retries.

